---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const withBase = (path: string) => `${base}${path.replace(/^\/+/, '')}`;

const toc = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'manual', label: 'Manual mode' },
  { id: 'paid-api', label: 'Paid API option' },
  { id: 'setup', label: 'Credential setup' },
  { id: 'troubleshooting', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="X Composer"
  description="Use ilyStream's X page as a manual go-live composer, with optional automatic posting only for users who bring paid X API access."
  slug="x-composer"
  updated="July 2026"
  readingTime="6 min"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    X changed its API economics. Free/developer access can authenticate an app,
    but posting can fail with credit or plan errors. ilyStream treats X as a
    composer-first integration: write the post in the app, copy/open it, and only
    enable automatic posting if you already have a paid X API plan.
  </p>

  <h2 id="manual">Manual mode</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Connect &rarr; X Composer.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Write your go-live post.</strong> Keep the stream link placeholder or paste the final link.</li>
    <li><strong>Copy or open the post.</strong> Publish manually in the X website/app.</li>
    <li><strong>Save your default text.</strong> ilyStream keeps the draft so it is ready between streams.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Manual mode is the recommended path for most users because it does not depend
    on X API credits.
  </p>

  <h2 id="paid-api">Paid API option</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a paid X API plan, open the collapsible section labeled for paid
    X API setup and connect credentials there. Automatic posting should remain
    opt-in and visibly separate from the normal composer.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free API</strong>: use manual composer mode.</li>
    <li><strong>Paid API</strong>: you may enable automatic go-live posts.</li>
    <li><strong>No credits</strong>: automatic posting will fail even if OAuth succeeds.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="setup">Credential setup</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Create an X developer app.</strong> Use the X Developer Console.</li>
    <li><strong>Enable user authentication.</strong> Choose OAuth 2.0 and allow tweet write permissions if your plan supports posting.</li>
    <li><strong>Add the callback URI.</strong> Use <code>http://127.0.0.1:8791/callback</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Paste client ID and secret.</strong> Add them to the paid API section in ilyStream.</li>
    <li><strong>Connect with X.</strong> Approve the account you want posts to come from.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p><strong>OAuth works but posting fails with credits depleted.</strong> That is an X plan/credit limitation. Use manual composer mode or upgrade the X API plan.</p>
  <p><strong>Access blocked during OAuth.</strong> Add your account as a test user or finish the X app user-auth setup.</p>
  <p><strong>Wrong account posts.</strong> Disconnect X, sign into the desired X account in the browser, then reconnect.</p>

  <div class="next-prev">
    <a class="is-prev" href={withBase('docs/chat-relay/')}>
      <p>Previous</p>
      <strong>&larr; Chat Hub &amp; relay</strong>
    </a>
    <a class="is-next" href={withBase('docs/audience-stats/')}>
      <p>Next</p>
      <strong>Audience profiles &rarr;</strong>
    </a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
